+# Why CVE-2025-69650 in `binutils` readelf Is a False Positive for Alpine 3.22 (binutils 2.44-r3)
+
+## Overview
+
+**CVE-2025-69650** is a double free vulnerability in GNU Binutils' `readelf`, reachable via the `--got-contents` option. The official description states:
+
+> `dump_relocations` may return early without initializing the `all_relocations` array. `process_got_section_contents` then passes an uninitialized `r_symbol` pointer to `free()`, causing SIGABRT.
+
+NVD tracks this against "GNU Binutils through 2.46" with CVSS 3.1 base score **7.5 (HIGH)** and **CWE-415: Double Free**. Security scanners flag this against Alpine binutils packages by name/CPE range alone, without checking whether the vulnerable code actually exists in the packaged version.
+
+NVD itself marks the CVE **disputed**:
+
+> "the observed behavior occurred only in pre-release code and did not affect any tagged version"
+
+Source-level inspection of the upstream `binutils-gdb` git history confirms this dispute and shows the vulnerable subsystem is entirely absent from Alpine 3.22's binutils package.
+
+---
+
+## Why Alpine 3.22 (binutils 2.44-r3) Is Not Affected
+
+### 1. The `--got-contents` feature does not exist in binutils 2.44
+
+The `--got-contents` readelf option -- and the `update_all_relocations` / `all_relocations` code this CVE targets -- was added upstream in commit `81e90cf63a10ad11772c2437c8f2a88f1a00c739` ("readelf: Add --got-contents option"), authored **2025-08-28**.
+
+Alpine 3.22's binutils package is built from upstream tag `binutils-2_44`, cut **2025-02-02** -- about seven months before that feature existed.
+
+```
+$ git merge-base --is-ancestor 81e90cf63a10ad11772c2437c8f2a88f1a00c739 binutils-2_44
+$ echo $?
+1   # not an ancestor -- the feature postdates the 2.44 release
+```
+
+### 2. Grepping the actual 2.44 source tree confirms zero matches
+
+```
+$ git grep -n "update_all_relocations\|all_relocations\|got-contents\|got_contents" binutils-2_44 -- binutils/readelf.c
+(no output)
+```
+
+None of the symbols this CVE describes exist anywhere in `binutils/readelf.c` at the `binutils-2_44` tag that Alpine 3.22 packages.
+
+### 3. The fix was never backported to the 2.44 line
+
+The upstream fix, commit `ea4bc025abdba85a90e26e13f551c16a44bfa921` ("PR 33698 and PR 33700 -- readelf.c (update_all_relocations): Zero array"), landed **2025-12-08** on `master` and `origin/binutils-2_46-branch` only. It was never cherry-picked to `origin/binutils-2_44-branch` -- because there is nothing to fix there. The vulnerable code does not exist on that branch either.
+
+---
+
+## Version Timeline
+
+| Event | Date | Commit |
+|---|---|---|
+| `binutils-2_44` tag (Alpine 3.22 baseline) | 2025-02-02 | -- |
+| `--got-contents` / vulnerable code introduced | 2025-08-28 | `81e90cf63a10` |
+| Upstream fix | 2025-12-08 | `ea4bc025abdb` |
+
+The vulnerable feature was introduced roughly seven months **after** Alpine 3.22's binutils baseline, and was fixed before it was ever part of a tagged release.
+
+---
+
+## Summary Table
+
+| Check | Result |
+|---|---|
+| Alpine 3.22 binutils version | 2.44-r3 (from tag `binutils-2_44`) |
+| Does 2.44 contain `--got-contents` / `update_all_relocations`? | **No** |
+| Is the feature-introducing commit an ancestor of `binutils-2_44`? | **No** |
+| Was the fix ever backported to `binutils-2_44-branch`? | **No** (nothing to backport) |
+| NVD status | **Disputed** -- "occurred only in pre-release code, did not affect any tagged version" |
+| Conclusion | **False positive** -- vulnerable subsystem is not present in this package |
+
+---
+
+## Recommendation
+
+Treat **CVE-2025-69650** as a **false positive** for Alpine 3.22 binutils 2.44-r3. No patch is applicable or required: the `readelf` code path this CVE describes does not exist in this version's source, so there is nothing to backport.
+
+---
